    </p>

    <pre><code>[SerializeField] private Sprite offSprite;
[SerializeField] private Sprite onSprite;

// Events to trigger things (like opening a door)
[SerializeField] private UnityEvent onLeverOn;
[SerializeField] private UnityEvent onLeverOff;

// ... later, inside Interact():
onLeverOn.Invoke();</code></pre>

    <p>
        Read those two event fields again and notice the word in front of them:
        <code>private</code>. That one word decides a great deal of this lesson, so hold on to it.
        Notice as well what is <em>missing</em>: the word "door" appears nowhere in that file. The
        lever has no idea what it is switching on. It flips a sprite, it fires an event — and who
        is listening is somebody else's business entirely.
